1
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:24,920
Riding the winds of passing seasons,
the shining greatest harem

2
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:37,580
Lightly leaping over the hectic times,
diving into the town, posing as yellow

3
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:39,660
I wanna die with you for the love

4
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:49,140
Like learning to wear only the quick things,
because the bare face decides the momentum

5
00:00:49,980 --> 00:00:51,040
Let it bleed!

6
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:58,240
Everybody can do,
the dream we set off running for never stops

7
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:03,440
Let's go regret again tomorrow! Let it wild!

8
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:07,660
Everybody can do, just a little

9
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:10,820
Even if we stick out, it doesn't hurt

10
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:15,020
Holding onto our rowdy curiosity

11
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:18,040
Strong and high, fly high

12
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:31,940
Foolproof method for
passing the Ryōshu-style test

13
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,760
Wow, that's nice

14
00:01:46,430 --> 00:01:49,680
TXR-002 Robo Jack

15
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:51,240
Forty thousand yen, huh

16
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:55,540
Even standing on my head,
I couldn't afford it, could I

17
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:57,180
Can't afford it, can I

18
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:03,020
I'm stone broke before payday, flat-out
cleaned out, with the money-shortage sickness

19
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:07,540
Oh crap!

20
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:08,260
Wait!

21
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:10,800
Hold on! Junpei, get up!

22
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:15,280
Honestly, you're such a nuisance
hanging around here again.

23
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:17,640
Junpei, aren't you going to study?

24
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:19,220
You have a test tomorrow, don't you?

25
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:22,580
Yeah, but even if I study now,

26
00:02:22,580 --> 00:02:25,260
it's not like I'll suddenly get smarter.

27
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:27,920
HAHAHA, well, that's true.

28
00:02:29,380 --> 00:02:29,560
Gig!

29
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:32,960
Honestly, a grown adult
joining in with kids like that.

30
00:02:34,140 --> 00:02:36,460
What's so great about that stuff, anyway?

31
00:02:36,580 --> 00:02:41,620
The ultimate masterpiece: a full-action
robot with 4-channel radio control.

32
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:46,020
Those who get it,
get it; those who don't, don't.

33
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:47,960
Is that so?

34
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:52,840
If only Junpei would at least
get around 80 on his test,

35
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:55,540
I'd gladly buy him that kind
of thing as much as he wants.

36
00:02:56,380 --> 00:02:57,100
Really?!

37
00:02:57,100 --> 00:02:58,940
You'd buy me as many as I want?

38
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:01,260
W-well, that was just a figure of speech!

39
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:04,420
You couldn't possibly get 80 points,
could you?

40
00:03:07,260 --> 00:03:08,320
Big brother...

41
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:09,720
Where there's a will, there's a way!

42
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:15,384
Look at this year's Nagashima Giants! They
overturned an 11.5-game deficit in the first half,

43
00:03:15,434 --> 00:03:18,160
and pulled off a miraculous
league championship!

44
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:21,120
When people are motivated,
they can do anything!

45
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:22,921
If Junpei gets 80 points on the test,

46
00:03:22,971 --> 00:03:25,360
you're really going to
buy him that RC car, right!

47
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:31,120
Well, I suppose so. Alright, it's settled!

48
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:34,140
Let's go, get ready, yokel!

49
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:39,040
Hey, hey, Ryo-san, Ryo-san, wait up!

50
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:44,300
Hey, hey, what are you doing, Ryo-san?
What are you going to do?

51
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:49,960
Leave it to me. But once we get that RC car,
you have to lend it to me for free too!

52
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,640
We're doing this, absolutely, once we...

53
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:02,120
A tutor?

54
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:05,300
What about being a tutor?

55
00:04:06,020 --> 00:04:07,480
Why would a senpai like him be doing it?

56
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:11,100
Can he even do it? Ryo-chan, tutoring?

57
00:04:11,100 --> 00:04:16,100
Hey! Don't underestimate me! What kind of
man can't handle elementary school homework?

58
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:18,200
Alright, let's get started!

59
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:20,880
Get started? The test is tomorrow, right?

60
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:24,780
That's why we're studying straight for 24 hours without sleep,
starting now.

61
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:27,740
That's crazy, you know.

62
00:04:27,740 --> 00:04:28,900
Crazy, schmazy. It works.

63
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:31,040
When I took my high school entrance exams,

64
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:32,960
I stayed up studying
for three days straight,

65
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:34,420
and I passed with flying colors!

66
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:36,460
Wait, you didn't sleep at all?

67
00:04:36,820 --> 00:04:38,660
Why would you do something like that?

68
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:40,700
If you sleep, you'll forget

69
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:42,240
everything you just memorized, won't you?

70
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:43,840
That's extreme.

71
00:04:43,840 --> 00:04:46,240
But the concentration of ordinary people

72
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:47,680
doesn't last that long, does it?

73
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:50,800
Yes, I've heard that even at work,
taking breaks

74
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:52,280
is said to be more efficient.

75
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:54,720
Naive! That's a story for mere mortals.

76
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:56,720
In my case, my endurance is different.

77
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:59,040
Common sense doesn't apply to me.

78
00:05:01,020 --> 00:05:03,920
It would be more accurate to
say I have no common sense, right?

79
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:05,620
Listen carefully.

80
00:05:05,620 --> 00:05:08,560
Normally, your pace gradually picks up,

81
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:10,580
and then it drops off, right?

82
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:17,220
But in my case,

83
00:05:17,220 --> 00:05:19,320
I start right at my peak.

84
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:22,860
And I carry it straight into exam day.

85
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:27,780
Your concentration really holds up well.

86
00:05:27,780 --> 00:05:29,180
I can't believe it.

87
00:05:29,180 --> 00:05:30,600
Where there's a will, there's a way.

88
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:35,280
Ordinary people think they're concentrating,
but they end up quite scattered.

89
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:39,860
In my case, every nerve from my brain
to my fingertips is focused on the test.

90
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:42,200
Mind, skill, and body are all at 100%.

91
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:44,940
But if I let my guard down even slightly,

92
00:05:44,940 --> 00:05:47,120
I'll drop straight down to zero.

93
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:49,840
I see, so it's like a
human-powered airplane.

94
00:05:49,840 --> 00:05:51,260
That's so like you, Ryo-chan.

95
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:55,260
So, starting now,
I'll begin the training my way.

96
00:05:55,260 --> 00:05:57,140
Where did those two go?

97
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:00,700
Whoa, that's amazing!

98
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:01,820
Found it!

99
00:06:04,020 --> 00:06:06,980
Just as I thought, my model kit I hid away!

100
00:06:06,980 --> 00:06:08,420
Hey, hold on there!

101
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:10,800
Stop it, you lot! Don't touch, don't touch!

102
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:14,540
Ryo-chan,
do you really think you're studying?

103
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:19,780
I understand your concentration, senpai, but that's
a separate issue from actual academic ability.

104
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:25,040
Honestly, how on earth did things get
twisted so that Ryo-san ends up being a tutor?

105
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:26,400
Well then!

106
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:28,780
How long are you going
to keep playing around?

107
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,520
Are you really going to study?

108
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:32,280
Going to?

109
00:06:32,940 --> 00:06:36,660
Of course! For my RC car,
I'd go through fire and water, wouldn't I?

110
00:06:36,660 --> 00:06:40,000
Come on, hand over the question sheets.
Where's the test range?

111
00:06:43,760 --> 00:06:46,100
Alright, let's start with the
Japanese language questions.

112
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:48,380
What's this?

113
00:06:48,840 --> 00:06:51,560
Answer the meaning of the following proverb.

114
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:53,520
Fifty steps, a hundred steps.

115
00:06:54,700 --> 00:06:56,200
What, that's easy, hey.

116
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:03,680
Well, obviously. Just say
"fifty steps, a hundred steps."

117
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:08,840
This is the starting line.

118
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,860
Alright, Junpei.
Walk a hundred steps from here.

119
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:13,560
Mm-hmm.

120
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:18,049
One, two, three, four, five,

121
00:07:18,099 --> 00:07:21,640
six, seven, eight, nine, ten.

122
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:25,160
Oh my, Ryo-chan.
It's dangerous to play in the road.

123
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:28,180
Grandma, this is studying. Studying.

124
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:29,220
Oh dear.

125
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:33,640
A hundred steps,
a hundred steps, fine, Ryo-chan.

126
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:33,720
Dad!

127
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:35,280
Alright!

128
00:07:35,540 --> 00:07:37,138
One, two, three,

129
00:07:37,188 --> 00:07:39,660
four, five, six, seven, eight.

130
00:07:39,660 --> 00:07:42,380
Ryo-chan, what do you think you're doing?

131
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:46,240
Right. Forty-six, forty-seven,
forty-eight, forty-nine, fifty.

132
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:47,640
Exactly!

133
00:07:48,060 --> 00:07:49,120
That's right!

134
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:52,910
So "fifty steps, a hundred steps" means that
even if it's a hundred steps for a child's legs,

135
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:55,440
it means an adult can
cover it in fifty steps.

136
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:56,480
Yeah, got it!

137
00:07:59,240 --> 00:08:01,520
I see, so that's another
way to interpret it.

138
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:03,320
That's ridiculous, obviously.

139
00:08:03,500 --> 00:08:04,980
Eye drops from the second floor?

140
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:06,720
Hey, hey, Ryo-san.

141
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:08,040
What do you mean? What do you mean?

142
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:11,280
Well, you just have to try it and see.

143
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:13,440
Here I go, Ryo-san.

144
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:15,220
Alright, that's good.

145
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:19,220
Aim carefully, now.

146
00:08:21,760 --> 00:08:24,340
I really do plan to put eye
drops in from the second floor.

147
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:36,800
Yay!

148
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:40,200
How about it? Ryo-san, get it?

149
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:43,660
Whoa, that's thrilling. Whoosh.

150
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:45,853
If you put eye drops in
from the second floor,

151
00:08:45,903 --> 00:08:48,440
the acceleration adds on and it feels great.

152
00:08:49,180 --> 00:08:50,300
Hey, Ryo-chan.

153
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:50,800
Yeah.

154
00:08:51,620 --> 00:08:53,720
That explanation is totally wrong.

155
00:08:54,420 --> 00:08:56,136
"Eye drops from the second floor" means

156
00:08:56,186 --> 00:08:59,720
something roundabout,
useless, and ineffective.

157
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:03,260
It's a proverb that came from China,

158
00:09:03,260 --> 00:09:05,120
about a man who fled fifty
steps on the battlefield

159
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:08,000
and how it's pointless to laugh
at a man who fled a hundred steps.

160
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,440
It means there's hardly any
difference between the two.

161
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:12,880
You're completely unfit to be a tutor.

162
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:15,260
Yes, hello?

163
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:16,760
Shut up, Reiko.

164
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:19,320
If you keep being so argumentative,
you won't be able to get married.

165
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:20,540
Is that right?

166
00:09:23,380 --> 00:09:25,020
Following a report from a neighbor,

167
00:09:25,020 --> 00:09:27,740
they're cracking down on
a vehicle parked illegally.

168
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:30,180
Reiko, could you come with us?

169
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:36,120
Okay? Ryo-chan, I'll be right back,
so don't teach him anything weird.

170
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:39,267
Alright, alright.
Hurry up and get to work, go on.

171
00:09:39,317 --> 00:09:41,320
Take your time, all right?

172
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:42,140
Geez!

173
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:46,700
Well, now that the noisy ones are gone.

174
00:09:47,640 --> 00:09:50,540
Don't hold back. If there's anything you don't understand,
ask away.

175
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:52,520
Here you go, Ryo-san.

176
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:53,380
What is it?

177
00:09:54,500 --> 00:09:55,640
What's a "Crane-Turtle Problem"?

178
00:09:56,580 --> 00:09:57,680
What? A Crane-Turtle Problem?

179
00:09:58,180 --> 00:09:58,500
This one.

180
00:09:58,500 --> 00:10:02,280
Let's see, what does it say?
There are cranes and turtles?

181
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:05,020
If you count the heads,
there are 20 in total,

182
00:10:05,070 --> 00:10:08,120
and if you count the legs, there are 62.

183
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:11,040
How many cranes and how
many turtles are there?

184
00:10:12,340 --> 00:10:15,530
Since cranes have two
legs and turtles have four,

185
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:21,440
It's for my remote-control car!

186
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:22,800
Give up!

187
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:24,580
Wait, I mean, cooperate!

188
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:31,140
Hey, Ryo-san. Did you catch the crane?

189
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:32,180
Hahaha.

190
00:10:32,420 --> 00:10:33,300
Shut up!

191
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:36,360
Hey! How about the turtle?

192
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:38,080
Look, there it is!

193
00:10:39,100 --> 00:10:41,200
Alright. That should be enough by now.

194
00:10:47,300 --> 00:10:49,760
Now, don't get mad.
It's a stand-in for the crane.

195
00:10:50,300 --> 00:10:51,740
Look, there's a turtle too.

196
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:54,100
Alright,
now finally the cranes and turtles...

197
00:10:55,180 --> 00:10:58,860
Whoa, hey! If you keep pulling on their legs,
how are we supposed to count them?

198
00:10:58,860 --> 00:11:04,140
Ugh, forget the turtles already!

199
00:11:04,140 --> 00:11:07,860
Counting! Counting, counting,
that's the most important study!

200
00:11:12,820 --> 00:11:14,040
So this is counting

201
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:20,180
That's right, a PET bottle rocket works by
using the law of action and reaction, you know.

202
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:27,320
The law of action and reaction means that whoever
applies a force receives that same force back.

203
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:32,980
If you pump a lot of air into a PET bottle
with water in it and blast it out all at once,

204
00:11:36,560 --> 00:11:43,900
the compressed air pushes out the water, and the bottle receives an equal force and flies off.
That's how it works.

205
00:11:43,900 --> 00:11:46,960
This is the same principle as a real space rocket,
you know!

206
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:50,720
Hey, Ryo-san, can't we make a bigger one?

207
00:11:51,380 --> 00:11:52,640
A bigger one!

208
00:11:53,840 --> 00:11:55,460
Alright, it's an applied problem!

209
00:11:58,660 --> 00:12:01,780
Alright, it's finished!
The drum-can rocket, the Ryotsu-go!

210
00:12:01,780 --> 00:12:04,080
Let's launch it already!

211
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:05,220
Alright, here goes!

212
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:25,120
Hey, you coward!

213
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:33,000
Ryo-san, are you okay?

214
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:34,180
I'm fine!

215
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:38,200
Alright,
let's move on to social studies next.

216
00:12:45,900 --> 00:12:48,840
Turn right at the alley,
and there's a temple symbol on the map.

217
00:12:55,500 --> 00:12:58,100
I didn't realize there were
so many symbols on the map.

218
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:00,360
Police boxes are marked with an X.

219
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:02,920
That's bad luck. I'd rather have a circle.

220
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:05,380
Circles are for ward offices
and town or village halls.

221
00:13:07,420 --> 00:13:08,760
A ninja mark!

222
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:11,960
Yeah, this one's the manji shuriken mark.

223
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:17,700
There are also cross, six-sided,
and eight-sided shuriken marks, right?

224
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:19,200
You really know your stuff, Ryo-san.

225
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:22,880
Of course. By the way, you can make
a cross shuriken out of origami.

226
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:31,740
There, all done!

227
00:13:31,740 --> 00:13:33,100
Cool!

228
00:13:33,100 --> 00:13:36,680
We used to make these all
the time and play ninjas.

229
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:41,320
Teach me!

230
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:44,840
Okay, first fold the origami paper in half,

231
00:13:49,340 --> 00:13:51,460
Nakagawa Keiichi, reporting back.

232
00:13:51,900 --> 00:13:53,880
Reiko Akimoto, reporting back.

233
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:55,740
Thank you for your hard work.

234
00:13:55,740 --> 00:13:57,940
How's the tutoring going?

235
00:13:57,940 --> 00:14:01,000
Yeah, it seems like they're working quietly.

236
00:14:02,740 --> 00:14:04,480
How about it, Ryo-chan? Making progress?

237
00:14:06,020 --> 00:14:09,580
Ne, de, shu, ne damn it!

238
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:10,587
You scoundrel!

239
00:14:10,637 --> 00:14:14,780
Ryotsu of the Fuma ninja clan won't
get hit by a wimpy shuriken like that!

240
00:14:16,740 --> 00:14:17,480
What's your problem!

241
00:14:17,660 --> 00:14:19,100
Hey, Fuma Ryotsu!

242
00:14:24,020 --> 00:14:25,460
Just as I thought.

243
00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:28,400
Because he's really just like a kid.

244
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:31,220
Fuma Ninpo: Scattered Shots!

245
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:34,040
Hey, Ryo-chan!

246
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:37,000
Ryo-chan!

247
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,800
You're back

248
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:43,120
Well, this is just...

249
00:14:45,700 --> 00:14:47,640
I've been hit!

250
00:14:48,900 --> 00:14:51,020
I thought so, but I got hit.

251
00:14:59,340 --> 00:15:03,320
History is easy. If you memorize it by rote,
you're guaranteed to get points, so.

252
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:04,080
Yeah.

253
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:11,740
What year was the Taika Reform again?

254
00:15:11,740 --> 00:15:13,660
What, the Taika Katsushin?

255
00:15:14,420 --> 00:15:17,740
No, it's Kaishin, the Taika no Kaishin.

256
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:20,520
It's 645.

257
00:15:21,140 --> 00:15:25,180
The way to remember it is
"Muji-ko no yoru-zukuri," so remember it as the Taika Reform.

258
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:30,180
I see. Now that you mention it, there was also "Hitonami ni ogore yo"
(Live it up like everyone else).

259
00:15:30,420 --> 00:15:32,640
That's a mnemonic for square roots.

260
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:33,460
Gah.

261
00:15:34,460 --> 00:15:36,240
Hydrogen, Helium, Lithium, Beryllium, Boron...
my ship.

262
00:15:36,320 --> 00:15:37,740
That's the chemical element symbols.

263
00:15:39,780 --> 00:15:41,852
There's also "Naku yo Uguisu, Heian-kyō,"

264
00:15:41,902 --> 00:15:45,540
and there's even
"Iyoku ni moeru Columbus," you know.

265
00:15:45,900 --> 00:15:46,720
Yes, that's the one!

266
00:15:47,260 --> 00:15:50,978
"Iyoku ni moeru Columbus,
" "Suikin chi ka moku,"

267
00:15:51,028 --> 00:15:53,960
"Dotenkaimei," "Kyōjin taihō," "Tamagoyaki,"

268
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:58,460
"Okane-da Hiro-oka, Okane-da Hiro-oka,"
what's that supposed to be?

269
00:15:58,460 --> 00:16:01,520
What on earth is that?

270
00:16:01,520 --> 00:16:03,300
What are you planning to teach the kids?

271
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:07,080
That's how I was taught when I was a kid. If you've got a problem with it,
take it up with the teacher.

272
00:16:07,780 --> 00:16:11,660
Hey, hey, you two are having all the fun over there.
Tell us too!

273
00:16:11,660 --> 00:16:12,560
Tell us!

274
00:16:13,580 --> 00:16:14,680
Sorry, sorry.

275
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:18,660
You remember that 645 was
the Taika Reform, right?

276
00:16:18,660 --> 00:16:21,980
Yeah, next is Ono no Imoko.

277
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:27,520
The one about
"Ono no Imoko ate sweet potatoes and went boo" was all the rage.

278
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:29,760
That brings back memories.

279
00:16:29,760 --> 00:16:32,120
So he ate sweet potatoes
and became a Sui envoy?

280
00:16:32,380 --> 00:16:33,500
A Sui envoy?

281
00:16:35,720 --> 00:16:40,040
Wasn't Ono no Imoko just the guy
who ate sweet potatoes and farted?

282
00:16:40,380 --> 00:16:43,180
So how on earth did he
end up in the history books?

283
00:16:43,180 --> 00:16:46,020
Because he was the first in Japan
to eat sweet potatoes and fart.

284
00:16:46,020 --> 00:16:47,720
Give me a break.

285
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:50,480
Well, that's pretty ridiculous.

286
00:16:54,580 --> 00:16:57,160
Wasn't there also a Kentōshi,
not just a Kenzuishi?

287
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:58,080
Yes, there was.

288
00:16:58,500 --> 00:17:00,740
It was about twenty
years after the Kenzuishi.

289
00:17:00,740 --> 00:17:03,120
There should have been
a Kentōshi ship, right?

290
00:17:03,530 --> 00:17:03,720
Yeah.

291
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:06,020
It's the ship they used to travel to China.

292
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:06,420
Right.

293
00:17:08,700 --> 00:17:11,240
Didn't that ship look like this?

294
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:13,680
The one with a lot of people rowing, right?

295
00:17:14,260 --> 00:17:14,640
Wow.

296
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:16,560
I think it was probably
shaped something like that.

297
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:18,740
Ryo-chan, you remember that really well.

298
00:17:21,180 --> 00:17:26,720
I remember doodling in my textbook, with
a U-boat firing torpedoes at the envoy ship.

299
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:28,000
Cool!

300
00:17:30,100 --> 00:17:32,960
But you remember even the
tiny details of the ships.

301
00:17:32,960 --> 00:17:35,160
I copied the ships over and over,
so I remember them.

302
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:37,600
I can draw the Kanrin Maru too.

303
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:42,920
The Kanrin Maru was a small wooden warship built in Holland,
about 50 meters long.

304
00:17:44,220 --> 00:17:47,320
I think it was used as a training
ship for the Shogunate navy.

305
00:17:47,320 --> 00:17:49,760
It had five cannons on each side, like this.

306
00:17:49,760 --> 00:17:50,860
You know a lot about it.

307
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:53,660
Someone sailed on this
ship to America, right?

308
00:17:53,660 --> 00:17:55,100
Who was it again?

309
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:57,520
Not Katsushin

310
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:58,540
It's Katsu Kaishu, right?

311
00:17:58,540 --> 00:17:59,740
Yes, that's the one.

312
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:03,500
You don't know any history,
but you remember the textbook illustrations.

313
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:05,000
I can draw people too!

314
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:06,500
How about Perry?

315
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:07,820
Perry?

316
00:18:07,820 --> 00:18:10,840
I think he looked like this.

317
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:11,900
Come on, give us some trivia.

318
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:12,560
Wow.

319
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:15,200
I think it looks like him.

320
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:16,900
How can you draw them so fast?

321
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:18,665
They were in the textbook, right?

322
00:18:18,715 --> 00:18:21,760
I always doodled like this during class.

323
00:18:25,240 --> 00:18:29,040
There was also Sugita Genpaku.
Drawn in ukiyo-e style, he looks like this.

324
00:18:30,220 --> 00:18:31,440
How about that? Pretty good, right?

325
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:36,260
Heads like this are the most fun to doodle on.
Back then, I used to get such a kick out of it.

326
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:40,840
Hey, Ryo-san,
can you draw Minamoto no Yoritomo?

327
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:41,820
What about Hideyoshi?

328
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:43,580
Of course.

329
00:18:47,840 --> 00:18:50,131
Kakeru kakeru. Jesus, Nobunaga, everyone,

330
00:18:50,181 --> 00:18:53,140
even Francis Xavier,
what a handful they are.

331
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:53,900
You!

332
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:57,840
Senpai, do you know who Sugita Genpaku was?

333
00:18:58,300 --> 00:19:00,920
Obviously, he was a rakugo storyteller.

334
00:19:01,220 --> 00:19:04,140
He's the man who wrote
the famous Kaitai Shinsho.

335
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:10,340
I figured from his face that
he was a rakugo storyteller.

336
00:19:11,260 --> 00:19:13,940
So he was the one who
wrote the Yajikita Dōchū-ki?

337
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:16,100
That's Jippensha Ikku, isn't it?

338
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:20,700
Well, I've certainly learned a lot.

339
00:19:20,700 --> 00:19:23,960
Don't blame me if we fail
the test because of this.

340
00:19:26,560 --> 00:19:28,360
And don't write that down.

341
00:19:33,300 --> 00:19:35,280
You've written that pretty well,
haven't you?

342
00:19:35,740 --> 00:19:38,280
That's because Ryo-chan
taught us something pointless.

343
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:40,340
You were impressed too, weren't you?

344
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:42,720
That's all for today's lesson.

345
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:44,440
Kin-konkā

346
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:46,020
What about the RC car?

347
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:48,020
Well, what can you do?

348
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:50,780
Honestly, this has gone way past mischief.

349
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:53,080
Ryo-chan, go bring them back.

350
00:19:53,080 --> 00:19:54,300
Me?

351
00:19:54,540 --> 00:19:58,180
Teaching them that they shouldn't do things
like this is part of their education, right?

352
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:05,000
Honestly, where did those guys go?

353
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:09,660
Those guys... could they possibly...?

354
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:16,240
What a disaster!

355
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:18,360
Hey, Ryo-san. Is it an incident?

356
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:18,980
Hey, shut up!

357
00:20:22,100 --> 00:20:23,360
Hey! Found you!

358
00:20:23,760 --> 00:20:25,180
Whoa! Ryo-san!

359
00:20:26,520 --> 00:20:30,320
You lot! Enough already!
Getting carried away like that, honestly!

360
00:20:30,820 --> 00:20:31,720
Sorry.

361
00:20:32,460 --> 00:20:34,220
Ryo-san, look, look!

362
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:35,700
I'm not falling for that!

363
00:20:35,940 --> 00:20:38,840
But look, it's exactly like your doodles,
big brother!

364
00:20:41,900 --> 00:20:42,540
Hey, that's...!

365
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:46,080
Hey!

366
00:20:46,080 --> 00:20:47,180
Hey! He's standing right behind me!

367
00:20:47,700 --> 00:20:48,400
I knew it!

368
00:20:49,140 --> 00:20:50,820
That bastard was in disguise!

369
00:20:51,140 --> 00:20:51,340
Haah!

370
00:20:52,600 --> 00:20:53,440
Gaaaah!

371
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:55,220
Wait, you!

372
00:20:59,020 --> 00:21:00,340
Damn you, I won't let you get away!

373
00:21:01,060 --> 00:21:02,060
Gaaaah!

374
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:05,300
Gaaaah!

375
00:21:10,580 --> 00:21:12,300
Yo, budget Japanese history!

376
00:21:15,380 --> 00:21:17,380
Bamu Shirotatsu, you're under arrest!

377
00:21:19,280 --> 00:21:21,320
H-how did you figure it out?

378
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:27,300
Well, that's a happy accident, isn't it?

379
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:32,160
It's nothing. I had a feeling
something like this might happen,

380
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:35,160
so I've been teaching those
kids the fun of doodling.

381
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:36,160
Aren't you a smooth talker?

382
00:21:36,620 --> 00:21:39,900
If the tests were perfect too,
we'd have nothing to complain about.

383
00:21:39,900 --> 00:21:42,300
You idiot, of course it's done properly!

384
00:21:42,680 --> 00:21:44,900
Who do you think taught them? Who?

385
00:21:47,240 --> 00:21:48,060
Ryo-san

386
00:21:51,100 --> 00:21:52,500
Look, look!

387
00:21:53,040 --> 00:21:54,660
Hey, 80 points!

388
00:21:55,560 --> 00:21:57,160
At best, 50 points.

389
00:21:58,100 --> 00:21:59,980
We're 30 points short, so how...?

390
00:22:01,100 --> 00:22:05,020
Because we helped catch a criminal, a
high-ranking police officer bought it for us.

391
00:22:05,460 --> 00:22:06,440
That's great.

392
00:22:06,940 --> 00:22:07,260
Yeah.

393
00:22:11,600 --> 00:22:14,900
Studying glued to a desk
isn't everything in life.

394
00:22:15,240 --> 00:22:19,040
My practical method of studying
is what counts as real learning.

395
00:22:19,040 --> 00:22:19,600
Yeah.

396
00:22:20,660 --> 00:22:23,420
Take our Chief, for example.
He studied single-mindedly,

397
00:22:23,420 --> 00:22:25,180
and that's how he ended
up with such a stiff head.

398
00:22:25,180 --> 00:22:28,180
Even when he watches TV variety shows,
he doesn't laugh or even get surprised.

399
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:29,660
He actually ends up getting angry about it.

400
00:22:29,980 --> 00:22:31,240
H-hey, hey, senior!

401
00:22:31,240 --> 00:22:31,980
What?

402
00:22:32,540 --> 00:22:33,940
Well, it's true, isn't it?

403
00:22:33,940 --> 00:22:36,880
No one can follow a stubborn
fool like that as a subordinate.

404
00:22:36,880 --> 00:22:38,960
He's just an obstinate old geezer.

405
00:22:38,960 --> 00:22:40,240
Shiroizu-kun.

406
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:43,880
C-Chief!

407
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:46,200
Yesterday you did a great job, didn't you?

408
00:22:46,720 --> 00:22:51,060
Working with citizens to arrest a wanted criminal,
you're an admirable officer.

409
00:22:51,540 --> 00:22:54,420
While you're at it, erase those doodles from
your so-called practical study method too.

410
00:22:54,420 --> 00:22:58,060
It would be a big help if
you erased them completely.

411
00:22:59,980 --> 00:23:03,740
Chief, you're always joking.
Those were drawn by these guys on their own.

412
00:23:03,980 --> 00:23:06,260
Stop your chattering and
go erase them right now!

413
00:23:06,520 --> 00:23:07,020
Hey!

414
00:23:11,680 --> 00:23:14,120
Why does this always happen to me?

415
00:23:14,660 --> 00:23:16,620
Ryo-san, I hear you did a great job.

416
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:18,440
Yes!

417
00:23:19,180 --> 00:23:21,940
Hey, you lot, help me out too!

418
00:23:22,820 --> 00:23:23,460
Yes!

419
00:23:23,560 --> 00:23:26,883
Ryo-san's off playing with his
remote-control car in the park, so

420
00:23:26,933 --> 00:23:28,620
come over once you're done with that.

421
00:23:30,080 --> 00:23:30,440
Damn it!

422
00:23:30,780 --> 00:23:33,360
Damn those kids...

423
00:23:33,360 --> 00:23:36,180
Ugh, this is ridiculous! I'm not doing this!

424
00:23:37,220 --> 00:23:38,016
Well,

425
00:23:38,066 --> 00:23:41,240
cleaning things up is fun, isn't it?

426
00:23:41,240 --> 00:23:44,122
Yo-tsu-kun, I forgot to mention earlier,

427
00:23:44,172 --> 00:23:45,638
the cost of the damage to our station,

428
00:23:45,688 --> 00:23:49,580
we've decided to deduct it from your salary.

429
00:23:49,580 --> 00:23:52,600
What? N-no way, Chief!

430
00:24:05,620 --> 00:24:09,160
Bonus, bonus, how happy I am,

431
00:24:09,160 --> 00:24:11,280
pay off my debts,

432
00:24:11,280 --> 00:24:14,960
no way!
This is money I earned by sweating blood!

433
00:24:14,960 --> 00:24:16,700
I won't hand it over to anyone!

434
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:20,600
See you in the next bonus battle!

435
00:24:29,980 --> 00:24:37,760
Even if you stop the clock,
time keeps moving on,

436
00:24:39,480 --> 00:24:47,980
so scowl and cry,
laugh it off, and keep living.

437
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:57,940
Even if today is rainy,

438
00:24:57,940 --> 00:25:03,440
tomorrow will be sunny.

439
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:08,620
Bye-bye, let's wave our hands,

440
00:25:08,620 --> 00:25:13,880
goodbye to the unpleasant things.

441
00:25:13,880 --> 00:25:21,460
Oh yeah, let's live the way we like.

442
00:25:21,460 --> 00:25:30,260
Good things will come.
The sun is calling you outside the door.

443
00:25:43,880 --> 00:25:44,000
Thanks for watching.

